"""ordinary-foldable-code.py <folder>: Ordinary code in which the build knows everything: a flag at the top of the file and
one use of it, dead branches, methods on literals, small helpers called with literals, constants made out of constants.
Nothing goes through process.argv, Date.now() or a helper that hides a value, and nothing is printed in front of the
constants: a compiler once crashed on `const isDev = false; const url = isDev ? "a" : "b"; console.log(url);` while it built
two thousand stored programs, and a single console.log in front of those lines hid the crash. One file a case. Left out:
`process.env.NODE_ENV === "development"` (an executable answers it at build time), the text of functions and classes, and
whatever throws.
"""
